{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452676-aberrant-post-your-character-ideas-and-systems-observations","id":1452676,"title":"[Aberrant] Post Your Character Ideas and Systems Observations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-17T12:50:43-07:00","id":1452676,"title":"[Aberrant] Post Your Character Ideas and Systems Observations","content":"I thought it might be worth it to start a thread to post character ideas. These and not completely done characters, but get most of the way there.<br /> <br /> <br /> After doing a couple characters, it turns out that the rule that each level of scale you have above an opponent lets you buy the inflict damage stunt one more time is extremely important. With three or more scales beyond an opponent being an auto success the game really encourages at least scale 3 defense. Interestingly while Quantum Attack and most defensive powers are scale = dots, mega-strength is scale = dots +1. I\u2019m not sure if this is a rules error or intended to encourage strength based attacks.<br /> <br /> <br /> The upshot of all of this, is that characters will want at least one, if not two, extra health levels to prevent being taken out by an alpha strike. Eufiber (on an attuned Kevlar Vest) does not appear to be adequate armor \u2013 though the game needs some armor stacking rules. If you could get the extra health levels from Eufiber plus a forcefield for soft armor and scale, that would make Eufiber very interesting.<br /> <br /> <br /> A couple things are overpowered. Quantum Deflection provides a flat increase to a defense score. With pools capped at ten dice, an attack roll is unlikely to generate more than four hits, meaning Quantum Deflection 4 or 5 (1+4 or 5 defense) makes it almost impossible to hit somebody without using an area attack. Many powers are more useful if you downgrade their duration from rounds to maintained. Additionally, powers with the inflict tag can be very strong. These roll Quantum + Power instead of X + Aim or Close Combat and can inflict instant lose conditions (teleported to the sun/another planet, turned into a frog, rendered completely immaterial or shrunk to a microscopic level all come to mind).<br /> That said, for most characters the game appears fairly balanced. Everyone is going to end up with around the same level of combat ability, with a couple of other abilities to help define the character (with the possible exception of social stat based builds).<br /> <br /> Codename: Cryptid<br /> <br /> Concept: Max Transformation/Combat Monster<br /> <br /> Origin: Adventure<br /> <br /> Role: Combat Specialist<br /> <br /> Society: Elite<br /> <br /> Intelligence: 3; Cunning 3; Resolve 2<br /> Might: 4; Dexterity: 3; Stamina: 3<br /> Presence: 3; Manipulation: 2; Composure 2<br /> <br /> Aim: 2; Athletics: 1; Close Combat: 5 (claws)<br /> Command: 1; Culture: 1; Integrity:2<br /> Larceny: 1; Persuasion: 2<br /> <br /> Edges: Hardy, Direction Sense, Precise Martial Arts (2), Wealth (2), Alternate Identity (1)<br /> <br /> Contacts: Come Back to This Later<br /> <br /> Quantum: 4<br /> <br /> Transcendence: 0<br /> <br /> Mega Stats: Mega-Composure 1 (Always Prepared)<br /> <br /> Mega-Edges: Overwhelming Denial 1 (Restriction, Only when in Cryptid Form (reduce cost to 6 points) )<br /> <br /> Powers: Transform 5 (Reduced Duration (Maintained), Restricted -1 (No Random Forms) Extra Traits 2)<br /> <br /> Technique 1: Boost 4 (Reduced Duration (Maintained), Extra Attribute 1, Variable)<br /> <br /> Technique 2: Healing 5.<br /> <br /> Restrictions: No random forms (-1). The form must be based on something. Cannot randomly add extra modifications (like Grayson). Cryptids (-2), on the other hand if the form is a Cryptid gain<br /> Overwhelming Denial.<br /> <br /> Example Transformation: a MFing Dragon<br /> Growth 3 (Mega Might 3), Body Modification 3 (Claws, Wings, Tail), Toughness 4 (Hard Armor 1,3 5)<br /> <br /> Notes: The transformation power was so broad I had to impose some limitations to keep it from swamping the character. Well, I cheesed the tags a bit, but the end result seems more like a decently good tank that can keep going with physical attacks for awhile.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve","name":"DrSteve","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T14:51:00-07:00","id":1452696,"title":"","content":"I would make boost 5 and have it be one at a time (from my reading you can activate it for other attributes in subsequent rounds (or as a mixed action)).<br /> <br /> Personally I would probably go for absorption rather than healing (help a bit with the tanking and takes care of the potential non-regeneration of Quantum points)<br /> <br /> Depending on how you are flavoring the transformation you could add molecular chameleon, quantum imprint, transmutation, or potentially heal (if you remove it in the 1st place). I would be very tempted to take a few transformations in order to add another technique (in this case I would add molecular chameleon) now you are transforming organic matter, inorganic matter, and energy.<br /> <br /> Also, if you boost first, you can easily bring your physical stats up to 5 (and some mega attributes), therefore giving even more flexibility to your transformation. If this is your plan, I would de-prioritize the physical stats.<br /> <br /> If you can manage to get the mega-speed or regeneration mega-edges (potentially through Q-tech) you could really go crazy (you could trade the mega-composure or something like that for Q-Tech (or attunement) you can easily get a rank 5 Q-tech item.<br /> <br /> The problem that I have with combining Boost and Transform is that it essentially makes your character fit for almost any role in a team. That being said, it I were to become a nova, something like this would be my fondest desire.<br /> <br /> I have also played with trying to create a &quot;Wizard/sorcerer&quot; with transmutation, Quantum construct, quantum anima, illusion, etc. relies heavily on the technique mega edge<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T20:21:46-07:00","id":1452733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrSteve</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452676-aberrant-post-your-character-ideas-and-systems-observations#post1452676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, powers with the inflict tag can be very strong. These roll Quantum + Power instead of X + Aim or Close Combat and can inflict instant lose conditions (teleported to the sun/another planet,</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're overestimating the combat utility of Teleport with the Impose Tag. While instantly removing an opponent from the field of battle (possibly permanently) sounds great, it is far less impressive in practice.<br /> <br /> First, you have to touch your target. Do you really want your teleporter getting into melee range?<br /> <br /> Second, you roll Quantum + Teleport, which will usually top out at 9 dice, since Teleport requires Dots + 1 Quantum.<br /> <br /> Third, you're rolling versus the target's Defense. Minor Threats from the Core book's Antagonists table (pg. 139) start with a Defense of 3. You're going to be missing with a lot of attacks unless you're targeting cannon fodder opponents.<br /> <br /> If you really want to put the hurt on enemies, go for Quantum Attack. Your attack dice pools can be bigger (and are cheaper to buy up to max), you gain Enhancement equal to Quantum/2 (so it hits more often automatically as you get stronger), extra dots provide scale (for more damage), and you get to add all sort of interesting combat Tags.<br /> <br /> If you absolutely must try to kill folks via a teleportation style attack, I'd start with levels in Warp (lets you transport others by default and grants incredible range), then buy the Technique Mega-Edge and use Quantum Attack as a space warping disintegration effect. Or just buy one level of Warp and spend your points on buying up Mega-Might so you can throw enemies through your Warp gate.<br /> <br /> xxx<br /> <br /> If you want to make a really interesting character concept, start with the Mega-Edge Detect (dimensional flux), Remote Perception (with a Tag to see through to the other side of a detected dimensional flux, if required by the Storyguide), and Warp. You're now running a Sliders campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","user":"Shepherdboi","date":". 06-17-2021, 11:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T05:03:40-07:00","id":1452757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>econclark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452676-aberrant-post-your-character-ideas-and-systems-observations?p=1452696#post1452696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would make boost 5 and have it be one at a time (from my reading you can activate it for other attributes in subsequent rounds (or as a mixed action)).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Boost only affects 1 attribute, chosen when you buy the power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p.208</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The nova channels forces to enhance one of their own Attributes, chosen when this power is acquired.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T05:46:50-07:00","id":1452762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452676-aberrant-post-your-character-ideas-and-systems-observations?p=1452757#post1452757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Boost only affects 1 attribute, chosen when you buy the power.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Right. If you want to be able to switch between multiple attributes, you take the technique Mega Edge along with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T05:52:23-07:00","id":1452763,"title":"","content":"Or the Extra Attribute tag if you don't want to use up your Technique slots. Or if you want to change each time, use the Variable Attribute tag.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T05:54:11-07:00","id":1452765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452676-aberrant-post-your-character-ideas-and-systems-observations?p=1452762#post1452762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right. If you want to be able to switch between multiple attributes, you take the technique Mega Edge along with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, you have the Extra Attribute tag and the Variable tag that can be used to get the result suggested.<br /> <br /> Edit: Florin was faster...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T07:18:14-07:00","id":1452769,"title":"","content":"yes, the variable tag is what I was suggesting. As far as I can tell you can just activate it 9 times once for each attribute and be fully boosted. If you need it a bit quicker, you can do a mixed action to boost multiple attributes at once (although it seems that you would have to pay the 1 quantum point surcharge for each time in a round after the 1st). Therefore boost (4-5) with a maintained duration or a long continuous duration and the variable tag can fairly easily have someone playing with effectively 5 dots in each attribute and a variable amount in each mega-attribute. It is extremely powerful.<br /> <br /> Countering this is the fact that it could be disrupted, and costs quite a bit (in terms of quantum points, rounds, and experience) to set up.<br /> <br /> If you combine this with Transformation you get several other benefits: 1. you can allocate physical mega-attributes up higher than you normally have your attribute rated. 2) you can allocate transformations to sensory mega-edges (without having purchased mega-cunning normally). 3. You generally won't allocate as many of the transformation to Mega attributes which allows more flexibility in terms of what else can be taken (more toughness, throw in some plasticity, etc). <br /> <br /> I am still trying to figure out exactly how many quantum points it takes to activate Transformation but it seems like sort of a lot (particularly after being boosted 9 times first) which is why I would suggest absorption with the siphon extra (and probably the broad extra). It does provide some extra defense (unless you do siphon only) but more importantly allows the easy recharging of Quantum points (one of the few ways to recharge if you have powers active between scenes, which you would probably want to for such expensive powers).<br /> <br /> Depending on your story guide, they may allow you to purchase mega-edges that would essentially use dots gained from boost or transform as &quot;prerequisites&quot; the mega-edges would only be available when you fulfill the prerequisites (they may have a restricted flaw only when boosted/transformed), but some that would really help are regeneration and mega-speed.<br /> <br /> Thanks to the boosting you can then fulfill almost any role on the team (except warper unless you have some Q-tech for that). You could fight, sneak(use shrink), invent (boost mega mental attributes), sense (transformation is really great for this).<br /> <br /> This set up can easily turn a character into a bit of a Mary Sue, however it does make the character a very good swiss army knife.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T08:09:25-07:00","id":1452777,"title":"","content":"If you already have a power active, can you activate it again? I'd say no, but I'm not sure the book has anything to say on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T09:07:53-07:00","id":1452789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452676-aberrant-post-your-character-ideas-and-systems-observations?p=1452777#post1452777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you already have a power active, can you activate it again? I'd say no, but I'm not sure the book has anything to say on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t think there is anything in the book about it, BUT if you think techniques are \u201cthe same power used in different ways\u201d and you can use multiple at same time it would define you CAN activate the same power multiple times (different form Psionic powers, that can\u2019t be activated if already active).<br /> <br /> What I would limit is using the same power to stack effects on the same target, like attack multiple times the same target in a round, activate many force fields around yourself to stack a huge soft armor value, force the target to resist multiple times your mega social edge, or anything in that direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T10:08:05-07:00","id":1452796,"title":"","content":"My knowledge on this is obviously shake, but I seem to recall that the whole point of the technique is it you can't have multiple techniques active at the same time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T10:30:03-07:00","id":1452801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452676-aberrant-post-your-character-ideas-and-systems-observations?p=1452796#post1452796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My knowledge on this is obviously shake, but I seem to recall that the whole point of the technique is it you can't have multiple techniques active at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you can even use multiple of them in the same round, that\u2019s where they differentiate from multiple powers. M&amp;M is where you can\u2019t use multiple powers of the same array at same time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T10:34:03-07:00","id":1452804,"title":"","content":"You can, you just have to pay a 1 quantum point surcharge on additional actions using the power suite in a mixed action. I am not 100% how that interacts with powers having a longer duration. ex. if you have a gravity controlling power suite with flight and quantum attack, if you activate flight in the first round, and then activate quantum attack in the 2nd round (with flight still active), do you pay the surcharge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T14:54:15-07:00","id":1452824,"title":"","content":"First of all, this is talking primarily about techniques and power Suites: adding a tag to a power does not make it a power suite, so I would not expect you to be able to activate boost while boost is already running. The extra attribute tag lets you boost multiple attributes with one roll, so the whole mixed actions thing is a non-issue there. The variable attribute tag let's you choose one attribute when you roll (or more, if you also took extra attribute) to boost. Since this isn't a power suite, I don't see being able to activate it a second time while it's still running on the 1st time. <br /> <br /> The mixed action rules assume that you're making a single activation roll. They do not normally allow for you to activate a technique while the power Suite is already running; the implication is that you don't get to activate the various techniques sequentially. If you already have techniques running and you want to add another, you need to start over.<br /> <br /> There may be some leeway in there for reaction, seeing as those are actions that can't be activated at will. I could see a ruling that <i>only</i> reactions can be rolled without having to restart the power Suite, and then only if you're willing to spend the point of quantum that the rules require. <br /> I would not extend that ruling to include actions that have no dice pools. Frankly, the only reason why they cost a point of quantum is because there needs to be something to offset what would otherwise be free access to a power; and my own inclination would be to require the expenditure of one success from the dice pool for the activation of a technique that does not itself have a dice pool, rather than requiring another point of quantum to be spent. That maintains the logic that the more technique you attempt, the fewer successes you have available for any one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-19T07:40:37-07:00","id":1452893,"title":"","content":"Can someone please give actual examples of how to buy powers using the Variable tag? I read the text, but couldn't understand how it works in practice. :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-19T08:10:54-07:00","id":1452897,"title":"","content":"Anova has a Quantum attack that operates a bit like a Star Trek phaser: he takes a variable tag that is either non-lethal or destructive. Non-lethal and destructive are both 2-point tags, so the variable tag starts out at two points. There are two configurations for it, which is one more than normal, so the tag is worth one more, making it a three-point tag.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-19T10:43:19-07:00","id":1452903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452676-aberrant-post-your-character-ideas-and-systems-observations?p=1452897#post1452897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anova has a Quantum attack that operates a bit like a Star Trek phaser: he takes a variable tag that is either non-lethal or destructive. Non-lethal and destructive are both 2-point tags, so the variable tag starts out at two points. There are two configurations for it, which is one more than normal, so the tag is worth one more, making it a three-point tag.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://tenor.com/FKH6.gif\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://media1.tenor.com/m/q07DHKhjEBQAAAAC/nazare-tedesco-nazare-confusa.gif\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://tenor.com/FKH6.gif\" target=\"_blank\"> Nazare Tedesco Nazare Confusa GIF - Nazare Tedesco Nazare Confusa Nazare - Discover &amp; Share GIFs </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://tenor.com/FKH6.gif\" target=\"_blank\"> https://tenor.com/FKH6.gif </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Click to view the GIF </div> </div> </div><br /> <img src=\"https://tenor.com/FKH6.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> THANK YOU Dataweaver, I finally got it!!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-19T11:19:41-07:00","id":1452905,"title":"","content":"I would say that each power is at the very least its own power suite (there may be others with it), so if you activate a quantum attack as a mixed action to attack multiple targets, you would have to pay the extra nova point. I extended this logic to my reading of boost. You can take the power tag, and do it all as one action, or you could do a mixed action applying to a different target (attribute) each time (and paying the extra point). Therefore, if you want to use it on subsequent rounds it would not be a mixed action. I wouldn't expect the same attribute to be able to be boosted twice by it, but it seems to me like each attribute would be a different target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-19T11:30:18-07:00","id":1452906,"title":"","content":"For mixed actions, you only pay the extra Quantum point if it is a reaction or a power that doesn't have a dice pool. Otherwise, it's just a matter of splitting the successes you rolled among the various actions you're attempting. And again, you can't \u201cmix\u201d actions over consecutive rounds: that's just using them one after another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-19T15:12:46-07:00","id":1452911,"title":"","content":"Codename: NovaElf FX Unlimited LLC a.k.a. Sarah (Master of Production Chaos)<br /> <br /> Concept: Push Transformations and Transcendence / Nova FX Aristist<br /> <br /> Origin: Suburbia<br /> Role: Technology Expert (Modified)<br /> Society: Project Utopia (Public Relations/Damage Control)<br /> <br /> Intelligence: 3; Cunning 3; Resolve 2<br /> Might: 1; Dexterity: 3; Stamina: 2<br /> Presence: 3; Manipulation: 4; Composure 4<br /> <br /> Culture: 1; Empathy: 1; Humanities: 1<br /> Technology: 3 (AV Production); Science: 1; Persuasion: 3 (Media)<br /> Integrity: 2; Aim: 3 (Quantum Anima)<br /> <br /> Edges: Wealth 2; Artistic Talent 1(2); Photographic Memory 3; Big Hearted, Fame 1, Attunement 1<br /> <br /> Attuned Device: A table that ads an additional dot of Artistic Talent.<br /> <br /> Contacts: Should definitely be added (later)<br /> <br /> Quantum: 5<br /> <br /> Transcendence: 3<br /> <br /> Transformation: Physiological Transformation: Elf (-6 Quantum Cost), Inhuman Beauty (-3 Illusion)<br /> <br /> Mega-Stats: Cunning 2<br /> <br /> Mega-Edges: Multitasking (1, Restriction (Does not apply to social rolls))<br /> <br /> Power: Illusion 5 (Inflict, you can cast Illusions on other people/objects);<br /> Technique 1: Quantum Construct 4 (Variable)<br /> Variant 1: Props (Multiple, Size 1, Durability 2, Subtle)<br /> Variant 2: Set (Selective, Size 3, Subtle)<br /> Technique 2: Quantum Anima 5 (Might 2, Strike, Manipulation, Maintained, Entangle)<br /> Technique 3: Quantum Field 5 (Hard Armor 1)<br /> <br /> Notes: So a Faerie with Glamour who works in Hollywood FX. Also has elfshot (strike on quantum anima). A different version might use Quantum Attack instead of Quantum Anima. The subtle tag on quantum construct means the ability to create things that look real, the inflict tag on illusion grants the ability to casts illusions on people/objects. The later may be a problem as it could impinge on both morph and maybe cloak. <br /> As far as power scale goes, hits hard and has a good defense. I tried the build doing five techniques and it just felt like the extra powers become superficial after a point (though quantum agent might be worth adding). <br /> On a side note, I worry that this character would end up being a cross between Loki and Eleven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve","name":"DrSteve","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-19T21:33:49-07:00","id":1452922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452676-aberrant-post-your-character-ideas-and-systems-observations?p=1452893#post1452893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone please give actual examples of how to buy powers using the Variable tag? I read the text, but couldn't understand how it works in practice. :/</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a bit confusing. Variable normally lets you have a set rearrangement of power tags, but boost has an ability specific tag called variable that lets you assign the boost to a floating power. While I think it might be possible to trigger a power with a duration of continuous(rounds) or longer multiple times on different attributes, this is probably not possible with the maintained tag (at least on a single target). While you could spend multiple turns powering up, this is only viable with a tag with continuous (hours) that would let you do it in advance of the fight.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to remind everyone that mega-stats are limited to no higher than the base stat. So if you want to add mega-might 3, you must have base might of at least three.<br /> <br /> While I could see a complete wild card character with Transformation, Boost, Molecular Chameleon, and possibly instant expert, I suspect this would be non-viable at most tables just based on the amount of time spent messing with it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve","user":"DrSteve","date":". 06-20-2021, 01:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve","name":"DrSteve","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T09:12:04-07:00","id":1452963,"title":"","content":"The limit for Mega-Attributes of them being no higher than the regular attribute (at least until 5), makes Boost even more powerful because it 1st increases the base attribute up to 5 and then if there is any leftover, increases mega-attribute. This means that if you boost your might 1st (you can bring it to 5 and potentially some mega-dots) and then use transformation to bring mega-might to 5 dots. The same logic holds for all the physical attributes. Social and Mental don't get the extra step from transformation, but they can still be boosted to 5 (base) and get some mega-dots just from boost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T14:41:42-07:00","id":1452992,"title":"","content":"One of my character ideas was a newly erupted nova on N-day who was still learning to control his powers based on the character from movie mortal (2020). I think the movie shows just the reaction everyone would have to novas on N-day including the novas themselves they would probably be just as scared and confused as everyone else. Well apart from the novas who erupt with some level of mega-intelligence, resolve or composure, those fortunate few would probably quickly go underground lay low and hide while waiting to see which way the wind ends up blowing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T18:44:20-07:00","id":1453003,"title":"","content":"Why would someone buy the Variable Tag, if you can do the same thing with Technique with a cheaper cost, and WITHOUT the limitation of Variable?<br /> <br /> eg:<br /> a) Quantum Attack, Variable (can be Destructive, or Non-Lethal). Variable is a level 3 Tag here. Limitation: I can't use both in the same round, can I? They are the same power!!!<br /> b) Quantum Attack Non-Lethal. Technique: Destructive. Cost = 1 Tag + 1 MegaEdge (Technique). I can use both in the same round with a mixed action.<br /> <br /> Is this correct, or I'm missing something? Why would anyone use Variable instead of Technique?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T21:11:17-07:00","id":1453010,"title":"","content":"Doesn't a 2-point tag, such as non-lethal or destructive, cost twice as much as a one-point tag? Going at it by way of technique would not be cheaper. Slightly more useful? Perhaps... But while technique lets you activate instances of the power with different configurations of tag, it does also force you to split your successes between them. Which mitigates how useful that is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T06:01:12-07:00","id":1453028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452676-aberrant-post-your-character-ideas-and-systems-observations?p=1453003#post1453003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would someone buy the Variable Tag, if you can do the same thing with Technique with a cheaper cost, and WITHOUT the limitation of Variable?<br /> <br /> eg:<br /> a) Quantum Attack, Variable (can be Destructive, or Non-Lethal). Variable is a level 3 Tag here. Limitation: I can't use both in the same round, can I? They are the same power!!!<br /> b) Quantum Attack Non-Lethal. Technique: Destructive. Cost = 1 Tag + 1 MegaEdge (Technique). I can use both in the same round with a mixed action.<br /> <br /> Is this correct, or I'm missing something? Why would anyone use Variable instead of Technique?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> One thing you need to keep in mind is your Quantum caps the number of Techniques you can buy. You may not want to tie up one of those slots with a second Quantum Attack when you can use the Variable tag instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T10:17:34-07:00","id":1453050,"title":"","content":"Codename: Dr. Magic<br /> <br /> Concept: Eccentric Wizard Detective<br /> Dr. of the Occult who believes that he is a wizard not a nova. Works as a consultant detective through DeVries. He is extremely arrogant considering himself a combination of Sherlock Holmes and Merlin. Very good, particularly when employing his \u201cMagic\u201d but not nearly that good in actuality. Is actually an OK fighter, but also a complete coward who would vastly prefer to flee or hide. If he feels relatively safe, he will attempt to incapacitate his targets and bring them in to complete his job.<br /> <br /> Origin: Life of Privilege<br /> <br /> Role: Detective<br /> Society: Elite<br /> <br /> Intellect: 4; Cunning 4; Resolve 2<br /> Might: 1; Dexterity: 2; Stamina: 2<br /> Presence: 2; Manipulation: 4; Composure 1<br /> <br /> Aim: 3; Close Combat: 3<br /> Enigmas: 5 (Occult);<br /> Larceny: 1;<br /> Persuasion: 3<br /> <br /> Edges: Eufiber (5), Attunement (3), Tough Cookie (2), Wealth (5), Fame (1), Keen Sense: Sight (1)<br /> <br /> Contacts: Come Back to This Later<br /> <br /> Quantum: 5<br /> <br /> Transcendence: 2<br /> <br /> Mega Stats:<br /> <br /> Mega-Edges: Q-Tech (1)<br /> <br /> Powers: Quantum Anima 5 (Duration: Maintained (1), Grab (1), Manipulation (1), ranged: Visual (1), Strike (1))<br /> <br /> <b>Power Staff (Rank 9 Q-tech (6 from Q-tech Mega-edge, 3 from attunement)</b><br /> Long walking stick made of an unknown material, with a crystalline looking turtle on the top.<br /> <br /> Melee (0), Reach (1), Shield (2)<br /> <b>Edges: </b> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px; width: 233px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">always prepared</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">1</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">library</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">danger sense</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">1</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">direction sense</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">1</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">iron will</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">ambidextrous</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">1</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">fast draw (staff)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">1</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">hair trigger reflexes</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">1</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">ms fix it</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">weak spots</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">1</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">striking</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">precise martial arts (staff)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">animal ken</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">1</td> </tr> </table></div> Quantum Powers:<br /> <br /> Elemental Mastery: Changing states<br /> Transformation (6): Ramp-up (-3), reduced duration (Maintained) (-1), extra traits (4), Impose (1), reflexive (2)<br /> Technique (5):<br /> <u>Transmutation</u> (6): Area (2)<br /> <u>Boost</u> (5): reduced duration: maintained (1), Variable Attribute (1), Bestow (1), extra attribute (2)<br /> <u>Absorption</u> (5): Broad (2), Siphon (1)<br /> <u>molecular manipulation</u> (5): area (2), range (1) <br /> <u>healing </u>(5): Range (1), area (2)<br /> <br /> Elemental Mastery: light/darkness<br /> <u>Shroud</u> (5): Broadband (1), Dual (1), Variable (1), range: Medium (1)<br /> Technique (2):<br /> <u>Quantum Field</u> (5): Intrinsic (0)<br /> <u>Phasing</u> (5): variable (1)<br /> <br /> Cost to activate = 10 Quantum points<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24929,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","user":"econclark","date":".  math error fixed 06-21-2021, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T13:44:15-07:00","id":1453074,"title":"","content":"Thick-Head<br /> Concept: Warrior<br /> Origin path: Street Rat<br /> Role path: combat specialist<br /> Society path: elite<br /> <br /> Attributes:<br /> Intellect 2; cunning 3; resolve 3;<br /> Might 3; dexterity 3; stamina 4;<br /> Presence 2; manipulation 1; composure 2;<br /> <br /> Skills:<br /> Survival 2, Athletics 3, Close Combat (unarmed combat), Aim (5)<br /> Edges: Tough Cookie 2, Armor expert 1, forceful martial arts (unarmed) 3, hardy 3, iron will 3, danger sense 1, wealth 2<br /> Quantum 5, transcendence 2<br /> Quantum powers:<br /> Plasticity 5<br /> Technique (3)<br /> Absorption 3(broad (2))<br /> Density 5<br /> Phasing 5 (variable)<br /> Transformations: Psychological shift (rage), feeding requirements (rocks, metal, concrete, etc), aberrant eyes (glow red when density is active), Anima Aura (theme song)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24929,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","user":"econclark","date":". 06-21-2021, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T13:59:31-07:00","id":1453078,"title":"","content":"The first one is fun and shows off some of the power and versatility of Q-Tech, (and the attunement edge, Q-Tech mega-edge).<br /> <br /> The second one show off just how crazy Density can be, Thick-Head essentially functions with mega-might 5 and toughness 5 (reflexively), so doesn't really have to prepare ahead of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T19:19:59-07:00","id":1453101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452676-aberrant-post-your-character-ideas-and-systems-observations?p=1453003#post1453003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would someone buy the Variable Tag, if you can do the same thing with Technique with a cheaper cost, and WITHOUT the limitation of Variable?<br /> <br /> eg:<br /> a) Quantum Attack, Variable (can be Destructive, or Non-Lethal). Variable is a level 3 Tag here. Limitation: I can't use both in the same round, can I? They are the same power!!!<br /> b) Quantum Attack Non-Lethal. Technique: Destructive. Cost = 1 Tag + 1 MegaEdge (Technique). I can use both in the same round with a mixed action.<br /> <br /> Is this correct, or I'm missing something? Why would anyone use Variable instead of Technique?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A couple of reasons to use variable. The first is that techniques let you reassign the XP and tags on the main power. So if you have a power to 5 and want to add a tag, other techniques in the power suite may end up picking up variable if they lack any more applicable tags. In addition, the limit of 5 techniques for a power can encourage use of variable. Quantum limits can be a factor. For example, NovaElf has Illusion at 5 but can only have 4 dots in quantum construct (Dots+1). I wanted her to be able to summon up the Adams Family house but also wanted her to be able to create a sportscar. Since that build is extremely XP tight, variable allowed me to shoehorn in an additional version of the power without spending additional XP","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve","name":"DrSteve","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T19:30:04-07:00","id":1453102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>econclark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452676-aberrant-post-your-character-ideas-and-systems-observations?p=1453050#post1453050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Codename: Dr. Magic<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Power Staff (Rank 9 Q-tech (6 from Q-tech Mega-edge, 3 from attunement)</b><br /> Long walking stick made of an unknown material, with a crystalline looking turtle on the top.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure you can combine the attunement and qtech edges into one pool of dots. Also, I think you are using techniques in a device.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The nova must meet all the prerequisites and<br /> requirements for the Technique\u2019s powers, and a<br /> Technique power cannot have an Experience cost<br /> greater than that of the base Quantum Power, although<br /> it may be less. This includes all of the power tags (positive and negative) associated with each power, but not<br /> any reduction in Experience cost for a power acquired<br /> with a transformation, since the Experience reduction<br /> for the transformation is assumed to apply to all of<br /> that power\u2019s Techniques as well. You do not spend the<br /> experience for the Techniqued Quantum Power, as<br /> the cost is covered by the purchasing of the Technique<br /> Mega-Edge </div> </div> </div>Since items have dots in power, not XP, it has no base XP and a technique cannot be taken on a power granted by an artifact.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve","name":"DrSteve","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T19:33:12-07:00","id":1453104,"title":"","content":"My first try with QTech. Not a takeoff on Dr. Magic, I designed all three characters a couple of days ago.<br /> <br /> Codename: The Alchemist<br /> <br /> Concept: Lots of Points from an Item / Iron Man<br /> <br /> Origins: Survivalist<br /> Role: Tech Specialist<br /> Society: Teragen<br /> <br /> Intelligence: 5; Cunning 3; Resolve 3<br /> Might: 3; Dexterity: 3; Stamina: 2<br /> Presence: 2; Manipulation: 2; Composure 2<br /> <br /> Aim: 3; Close Combat: 2; Technology: 4<br /> Science: 3; Integrity: 2; Culture 1<br /> <br /> Edges: Always Prepared, Iron Will, Weak Spots, Library (Chemistry/Alchemy), Chrysalis, Eufiber (1, hard Armor 1), Fame(1)<br /> <br /> Quantum: 5<br /> <br /> Transcendence: 1<br /> <br /> Transformation: Minor Anima Aura (Quantum)<br /> <br /> Maga-Stats: Mega-Intelligence 3 (Photographic Memory 2, Speed Reading 1)<br /> <br /> Mega-Edges: Q-Tech (2), Foresight (1), Instant Expert (1), Quantum Sense (1)<br /> <br /> Q-Tech: The Philosopher\u2019s Stone (Rank 7)<br /> Philosopher\u2019s Stone Powers: Transmute (4), Molecular Chameleon 5 (Reduce Duration (Maintained), Extra Traits(1)), Mega-Resolve 2 (Intrinsic), Regeneration 1*<br /> Philosopher\u2019s Stone Edges: Wealth (5), Hardy (3), Striking (2), Touch Cookie (2), Direction Sense (1), Lightning Calculator (1)<br /> Tags: Intrinsic Power<br /> Enhancement Bonus: 4 (Chemistry/Alchemy Roles).<br /> * It might be more fitting with the legends of the Philosopher\u2019s Stone if the character was actually immortal and will regenerate from just about anything \u2013 including being taken out (given enough time).<br /> <br /> Notes: Well this character might turn elements of the setting on its head. The western tradition has a lot to say about various idea of ascension and transcendence. So how is the racist Terant philosophy going to deal with the various idea of refining the soul found in alchemy?<br /> <br /> System wise, its a mega-int character getting powers from a device. In this case the power itself is broad, instead of using the modular power rules. Surprisingly has about the same power level as the other characters, with the mega edges being about equal to a third power with a technique. I\u2019d also like to note that how difficult it is to build a crafting character unless almost all points go into crafting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve","name":"DrSteve","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T08:12:40-07:00","id":1453165,"title":"","content":"I think that the reading of no technique mega edge for Q-tech is quite narrow. Q-tech does get dots rather than XP, but we know the dot-to-XP conversion. The only thing this really prevents in my reading of it is the Q-tech taking transformations or transcendence to reduce the XP cost....which makes perfect sense. It also is much easier to allocate dots to different things rather than XP (particularly when for some of the dots they could be either a quantum power (12 XP or an edge (3 XP).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T10:41:49-07:00","id":1453180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrSteve</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452676-aberrant-post-your-character-ideas-and-systems-observations?p=1453104#post1453104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quantum: 5<br /> <br /> Transcendence: 1</div> </div> </div> </div>Shouldn't Q5 mean Transcendence 2?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T10:54:10-07:00","id":1453184,"title":"","content":"it's quite a long time ago that I've read the Q-tech rules. If I remember right, you can craft them using only dice rolls (provided you have the Mega Intellect needed), right? So, you don't &quot;buy&quot; Q-Tech powers with XP, do you? I'm confused cause the &quot;Modular&quot; Tag talks about buying Q-Tech Powers as if they were normal quantum powers...<br /> <br /> can anyone explain to me &quot;Purchasing Q-Tech with XP in the same way you buy normal Quantum Powers?&quot; when it can (or should) be done, or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T12:26:52-07:00","id":1453195,"title":"","content":"You can &quot;Purchase&quot; powers with the modular tag in order to make them modules. This seems like it would be very little use except for a few exceptions (1. if you want to power to be intrinsic, 2. if you want to be able to improve the power in the module without rebuilding it, 3. you aren't good enough at crafting/mega int to make it yourself). Generally speaking it probably isn't worth the cost of the power tag to do it though.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I would just use the crafting rules to make modules (it specifies how). Which is where the true power/versatility of Q-tech lies. I created the Q-tech above without modules specifically to avoid this issue (it does not state that you start with modules, but it could very well be the case). A good crafter could probably take care of the whole group.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T23:44:42-07:00","id":1453247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>econclark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452676-aberrant-post-your-character-ideas-and-systems-observations?p=1453165#post1453165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the reading of no technique mega edge for Q-tech is quite narrow. Q-tech does get dots rather than XP, but we know the dot-to-XP conversion. The only thing this really prevents in my reading of it is the Q-tech taking transformations or transcendence to reduce the XP cost....which makes perfect sense. It also is much easier to allocate dots to different things rather than XP (particularly when for some of the dots they could be either a quantum power (12 XP or an edge (3 XP).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If I were SGing I might let a character buy techniques for the Qtech Mega-Edge (learning how to better use the device), but using device dots to purchase techniques on an items powers just strikes me as pushing things too far (and drastically cutting the value of modular powers).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve","name":"DrSteve","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T23:47:24-07:00","id":1453249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452676-aberrant-post-your-character-ideas-and-systems-observations?p=1453180#post1453180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shouldn't Q5 mean Transcendence 2?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's one point of transcendence for each point above four, and Cryptid doesn't have any transcendence from buying things at character creation, so I think T1 is correct (that's intentional so that the character can be used in an espionage game with Boost being the most important power and transformation being secondary).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve","name":"DrSteve","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T23:54:19-07:00","id":1453250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>econclark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452676-aberrant-post-your-character-ideas-and-systems-observations?p=1453195#post1453195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can &quot;Purchase&quot; powers with the modular tag in order to make them modules. This seems like it would be very little use except for a few exceptions (1. if you want to power to be intrinsic, 2. if you want to be able to improve the power in the module without rebuilding it, 3. you aren't good enough at crafting/mega int to make it yourself). Generally speaking it probably isn't worth the cost of the power tag to do it though.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I would just use the crafting rules to make modules (it specifies how). Which is where the true power/versatility of Q-tech lies. I created the Q-tech above without modules specifically to avoid this issue (it does not state that you start with modules, but it could very well be the case). A good crafter could probably take care of the whole group.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My thought was to have a device with modular powers and use Quantum Agent so that you can select with powers you want to agent to have. I figure you could flavor it as either a magician summoning demons or something like a rigger in Shadowrun (maybe using horde).<br /> <br /> I really think the modular rules are there just to give a crafter something to do, so that you are not just buying mega-int as a stat to provide background that will never be used again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve","name":"DrSteve","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T05:00:49-07:00","id":1453262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrSteve</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1452676-aberrant-post-your-character-ideas-and-systems-observations?p=1453249#post1453249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's one point of transcendence for each point above four,</div> </div> </div> </div>No it isn't. Page 90:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Quantum:</span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> A nova gains a point of </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Transcendence upon gaining their fourth </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">dot in the Quantum Trait, and another for </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">each additional dot in Quantum thereafter, </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">so a nova with Quantum 8, for example, has a </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Transcendence rating of at least 5.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T10:10:25-07:00","id":1453295,"title":"","content":"@Dr. Steve,<br /> <br /> I would actually be more hesitant to allow players to take Technique for Q-tech for 2 reasons.<br /> 1. the piece of Q-Tech is subject to change (including being lost/stolen/replaced<br /> 2. if you think about a rank 9 item, they may be tempted to put 20 dots into one power and then buy some techniques, this could lead to some crazy things (think hordes of Quantum agents), Transformation 9 with 5 extra attribute tags, reflexive, increased duration, impose...you can really start getting crazy at that point.<br /> <br /> Modules still have plenty of space to shine even if you allow the device to have the Technique mega-edge (it is NOT the most powerful or optimal choice for Q-tech, modules are actually better). For instance Mega-Attributes and Mega Edges are still left only to modules. In addition, They player may want other powers and/or run out of techniques. Finally, if truly &quot;optimizing&quot; the Q-tech structure, the piece of Q-tech is likely best off being made with only mega-edges that have one dot (that you always want), and having the ones that you want with high dots, mega attributes, and powers put into modules (a rank 9 device can have up to 40 modules, so technically your best bet would be to go all modules!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}